# Vercel serves the viewer as static files only: the viewer (web/), site data (data/sites/) and v0.1.
# Everything else stays off the server. Never upload keys.
.env
.env.*
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
twin/
tests/
tools/
data/raw/
serve.py
requirements.txt
README.md
*.sigmf-data
*.iq
# Runs that stay on your own machine (git-ignored) are not deployed either; the deploy matches the repo.
# The 12 replays (replay-*, replays.json) and the committed demo runs are deployed.
web/runs/hays-2026*
web/runs/hays-baseline-mavic.*
web/runs/hays-upgraded-mavic.*
web/runs/seed-m210-crs-only.*
web/runs/seriesA-mavic.*
web/runs/sweeps/custom-*
# Vercel Hobby caps a CLI upload at 100 MB. The range-Doppler files (.bin, ~200 MB) only feed the raw radar
# view under "Technical details"; without them every replay still plays (the viewer says so in that panel).
web/runs/*.bin
